<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29812" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūgītus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				lowing, bellowing</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mugitusque boum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 470</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">edere,</span>”
				<i>to utter lowings, to low</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 597</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					1, 560</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tollere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 2, 223</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a bellowing,
				rumbling, roaring, loud noise</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mugitus terrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nemorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 35, 86, § 360</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 10, 263</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labyrinthi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 1,
					53</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
